"stipulation-settlement-agreement (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/forms-and-filings/stipulation-settlement-agreement.pdf)\nciteturn1466view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 4; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":503}); Total lines: 158\nL0@P0: Form Approved for Optional Use\nL1@P0: L-3052A [New. 02/05/2026] STIPULATION - SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT PAGE ___ OF ___\nL2@P0: ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY: STATE BAR NUMBER:\nL3@P0: NAME:\nL4@P0: FIRM NAME:\nL5@P0: STREET ADDRESS:\nL6@P0:  STATE: CITY: ZIP CODE:\nL7@P0: TELEPHONE NO.:\nL8@P0: E-MAIL ADDRESS:\nL9@P0: ATTORNEY FOR (name):\nL10@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL11@P0: SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF ORANGE\nL12@P0: JUSTICE CENTER:\nL13@P0: Lamoreaux – 341 The City Drive, Orange, CA 92868-3205\nL14@P0: Central – 700 Civic Center Dr West, Santa Ana, CA 92701-4045\nL15@P0: PETITIONER/PLAINTIFF:\nL16@P0: RESPONDENT/DEFENDANT:\nL17@P0: CLAIMANT:\nL18@P0: CASE NUMBER:\nL19@P0: ☐ STIPULATION AND ORDER\nL20@P0: ☐ SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT\nL21@P0: ☐ STIPULATION TO FURTHER JUDGMENT ON RESERVED ISSUES\nL22@P0: ☐ OTHER\nL23@P0: RELATED CASE NUMBER:\nL24@P0: COURTROOM/DEPT NO.\nL25@P0: HEARING DATE\nL26@P0: CONTINUANCE DATE/TIME\nL27@P0: Respondent’s filing fee ☐ Paid ☐ Not paid\nL28@P0: INSTRUCTIONS FOR USE OF THIS FORM:\nL29@P0: This form is provided in three sections:\nL30@P0: Part A (4 pages) includes this title page and a signature page which is required in all cases, and also provides for\nL31@P0: agreements for restraining orders, attorney fees, judgment, and other orders.\nL32@P0: Part B (9 pages) provides for agreements for parentage, child custody and child, spousal, and family support orders.\nL33@P0: Part C (5 pages) provides for agreements for property division orders.\nL34@P0: USE ONLY THOSE PAGES THAT ARE NECESSARY FOR YOUR AGREEMENTS.\nL35@P0: NUMBER THE PAGES CONSECUTIVELY WITH THE SIGNATURE PAGE AT THE END.\nL36@P0: THE PARTIES AGREE TO THE FOLLOWING MATTERS, WHICH SHALL BE THE ORDERS OF THE COURT.\nL37@P0: ☐ TEMPORARY ORDERS PENDING JUDGMENT OR FURTHER COURT ORDER (PENDENTE LITE)\nL38@P0: The orders agreed to herein shall stay in effect until superseded by judgment or further order of the Court, whichever\nL39@P0: first occurs, and all other orders made in this case shall remain in full force and effect except as otherwise provided\nL40@P0: herein.\nL41@P0: ☐ SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT\nL42@P0: The orders agreed to herein shall be included in a judgment or further judgment to be filed herein.\nL43@P0: ☐ MODIFICATION\nL44@P0: The orders agreed to herein modify the prior orders and/or the judgment made in this case.\nL45@P0: All other orders made in this case shall remain in full force and effect except as provided herein.\nL46@P0: The judgment in this case was filed on ______. The last order modified hereby was filed on ______.\nL47@P0: NOTICE AND OPPORTUNITY TO BE HEARD (Mandatory for custody orders under Family Code section 3048a): The\nL48@P0: parties understand that they have the right to advance notice of court proceedings and an opportunity to be heard by the\nL49@P0: court, including the rights to present evidence, cross examine witnesses and argue, and by signing this agreement, waive\nL50@P0: any right to further notice and opportunity to be heard for the purpose of the validity of court orders made from this\nL51@P0: agreement.\nL52@P0: RESTRAINING ORDERS:\nL53@P0: 1. ☐ The STANDARD RESTRAINING ORDERS on the summons are terminated (Family Code sections 233 and\nL54@P0: 2040).\nL55@P0-1: 2. PROPERTY RESTRAINING ORDERS: ☐ Petitioner ☐ Respondent:DATE: CASE NAME: CASE NUMBER:\nL56@P1: Form Approved for Optional Use\nL57@P1: L-3052A [New. 02/05/2026] STIPULATION - SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT PAGE ___ OF ___\nL58@P1: ☐ Shall not transfer, encumber, hypothecate, conceal or in any way dispose of any property, real or personal,\nL59@P1: whether community, quasi community, or separate, except in the usual course of business or for the necessities\nL60@P1: of life.\nL61@P1: ☐ Shall notify the other of proposed extraordinary expenditures and shall provide an accounting of such to the\nL62@P1: court.\nL63@P1: ☐ Shall not cash in, borrow against, cancel, transfer, dispose of, or change the beneficiaries of any insurance or\nL64@P1: other coverage including life, health, automobile and disability held for the benefit of the parties or any minor\nL65@P1: child.\nL66@P1: ☐ Shall not incur debts or liabilities for which the other may be held responsible, other than for the necessities of\nL67@P1: life.\nL68@P1: ☐ Other/Exceptions:\nL69@P1: TEMPORARY PROPERTY CONTROL ORDERS:\nL70@P1: 3. ☐ Petitioner ☐ Respondent shall have the temporary use, possession and control of the following property:\nL71@P1: 4. ☐ Petitioner ☐ Respondent shall have the temporary use, possession and control of the following property:\nL72@P1: SEPARATE STIPULATION RE WAIVER OF FINAL DECLARATION OF DISCLOSURE (Family Code section 2105,\nL73@P1: Optional):\nL74@P1: 5. ☐ The parties waive the requirements of Family Code section 2105(a) for service on the other of a final\nL75@P1: declaration of disclosure and make the following representations:\nL76@P1: a) Both parties have complied with Family Code section 2104 and the preliminary declarations of disclosure\nL77@P1: have been completed and exchanged.\nL78@P1: b) Both parties have completed and exchanged a current income and expense declaration, that includes all\nL79@P1: material facts and information regarding that party’s earnings, accumulations, and expenses.\nL80@P1: c) Both parties have fully complied with Family Code section 2102 and have fully augmented the\nL81@P1: preliminary declarations of disclosure, including disclosure of all material facts and information regarding\nL82@P1: the characterization of all assets and liabilities, the valuation of all assets that are contended to be\nL83@P1: community property or in which it is contended the community has an interest, and the amounts of all\nL84@P1: obligations that are contended to be community obligations or for which it is contended the community\nL85@P1: has liability.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nstipulation-settlement-agreement-b (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/forms-and-filings/stipulation-settlement-agreement-b.pdf)\nciteturn1466view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 9; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":504}); Total lines: 374\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nstipulation-settlement-agreement-c (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/forms-and-filings/stipulation-settlement-agreement-c.pdf)\nciteturn1466view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 5; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":505}); Total lines: 103\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nL-3047 - Stipulation and Order Form Family Law (Fillable Form version) (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/forms-and-filings/stipulation-and-order-family-law.pdf)\nciteturn1466view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":506}); Total lines: 65\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - Stipulation - Participate in Voluntary Settlement Conference Rev 6-20-14 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l221.pdf)\nciteturn1466view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 1; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":507}); Total lines: 57\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nl967 (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l967.pdf)\nciteturn1466view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yester